Let $(X,\|\cdot\|)$ be a real normed plane (a two-dimensional real Banach space), with unit sphere $S_X = \{x \in X : \|x\|=1\}$. Fix an orientation on $X$ and denote by $u \wedge v$ the corresponding signed area (wedge) of an ordered pair $(u,v)$, so that $u \wedge v > 0$ means $(u,v)$ is positively oriented.

Recall the following orthogonality relations for $u,v \in X \setminus \{0\}$:
\begin{itemize}
\item Birkhoff–James orthogonality: $u \perp_B v$ iff $\|u + tv\| \ge \|u\|$ for every $t \in \mathbb{R}$.
\item Pythagorean-minus orthogonality: $u \perp_{P-} v$ iff $\|u - v\|^2 = \|u\|^2 + \|v\|^2$.
\item Pythagorean-plus orthogonality: $u \perp_{P+} v$ iff $\|u + v\|^2 = \|u\|^2 + \|v\|^2$.
\end{itemize}

For each orthogonality type $\perp_\ast \in \{\perp_B,\ \perp_{P-},\ \perp_{P+}\}$, define the associated Joly curve as the planar curve
$$
S_\ast \;=\; \{\,u + v \,:\, u,v \in S_X,\ u \perp_\ast v,\ u \wedge v > 0\,\}.
$$
So $S_B$, $S_{P-}$, $S_{P+}$ are the Joly curves built from positively oriented unit pairs that are Birkhoff, Pythagorean-minus, and Pythagorean-plus orthogonal, respectively.

It is known that:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $S_B = S_{P-}$ if and only if every $u,v \in S_X$ with $u \perp_B v$ and $u \wedge v > 0$ also satisfies $u \perp_{P-} v$.
\item[(ii)] $S_B = S_{P+}$ if and only if every $u,v \in S_X$ with $u \perp_B v$ and $u \wedge v > 0$ also satisfies $u \perp_{P+} v$.
\end{itemize}

Question: Can the orientation hypothesis $u \wedge v > 0$ be removed from the right-hand conditions in (i) and (ii)? Equivalently, is it true that
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i$'$)] $S_B = S_{P-}$ if and only if every $u,v \in S_X$ with $u \perp_B v$ satisfies $u \perp_{P-} v$;
\item[(ii$'$)] $S_B = S_{P+}$ if and only if every $u,v \in S_X$ with $u \perp_B v$ satisfies $u \perp_{P+} v$?
\end{itemize}

